---
description: Rules for simulation, physics and GPU code
globs: src/sim/**,src/domain/**,src/render/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- No imports from React or `src/app` in these folders.
- The model is a 2.5D thin film (lubrication approximation) on a grid. See docs/PLAN.md section 2 before changing equations.
- Sim units are the consistent **mm–g–s** system: length mm, mass g, time s, so pressure = Pa, viscosity = Pa·s, surface tension = mN/m (g/s²), density = g/mm³. Never mix in N/m or g/ml inside sim math; convert at the domain boundary. Document units on every physical parameter in `src/domain/physics.ts`.
- Colors in the domain are sRGB 0–1; convert to linear before blending or lighting.
- Each physics compute pass has a matching CPU function in `src/sim/cpu/` and a Vitest test. At minimum, test: total paint volume is conserved (except for edge drain), no NaN/Inf after N steps, and a symmetric initial state stays symmetric.
- Color/layer advection must be low-diffusion (BFECC or MacCormack with limiter). Never use plain semi-Lagrangian alone for color.
- Clamp timesteps for stability (CFL plus the h³ diffusion limit). Use substeps instead of hoping.
- Randomness only through the seeded RNG in `src/sim/rng.ts`. Pass seeds to the GPU as uniforms.
- Use ping-pong textures/buffers with explicit names (`heightA/heightB`). Don't read and write the same resource in one pass.
